name pair-2v2-f16-1
timeout 600

# THE SYMMETRIC FORMATION REFERENCE CASE: an F-16 element against an F-16 element, everything else
# equal. It is to doc/formation.md what duel-headon.fbm is to doc/duels.md — the case in which the two
# sides differ in NOTHING, so whatever the run produces is a property of the FLIGHT logic and not of
# the airframes.
#
# WHAT IS DECLARED, and it is the whole new mechanism:
#   flight <name> <position>   position 1 = lead, 2 = wingman. It is IDENTITY, like `team`: the
#                              cooperative datalink reads it off the registry and it makes the FL
#                              contact filter a statement instead of a mission-file ordinal.
#   datalink on                the flight's ONLY channel. Every piece of cooperation below travels in
#                              the PPLI both members already transmitted: the position report, the
#                              flight position, and a target POINT with a "still needs me" bit.
#                              Nobody ever learns WHO another jet sees (core/FBRadarContact is
#                              anonymous) — only WHERE it is pointed, correlated against one's own
#                              echoes and sometimes not correlated at all.
#
# GEOMETRY: 110 km apart on 46.90 N, co-altitude 8,000 m, head-on, both flights outside their own
# 40 nm radar gate at t=0 so both runs begin with a real search. Each wingman spawns ON its station
# (1 nm abeam on the right of its lead's track, 150 m stacked) so the run measures station HOLDING
# rather than station capture.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 (TIMEOUT) with all four alive is the expected verdict and NOT a missing answer —
# this is duel-headon's stalemate with two aircraft a side, and the subject is the SORT, not the kill.
# What the file measures is in the telemetry, one column set per unit (flt_*, doc/formation.md 8):
#   flt_assign      which track this jet is prosecuting. Two jets of one flight carrying the SAME
#                   non-zero value at the same time is a double engagement — the thing that must not
#                   happen while another contact is free
#   flt_dup         exactly that, as a flag: it must stay 0 wherever flt_free > 0
#   flt_free        contacts in this jet's own picture that nobody in its flight is on
#   flt_switch      how often the assignment changed. A number that keeps climbing is chatter
#   flt_sta         the wingman's station error in metres while it is holding, -1 while it is not
#   flt_both_s      seconds in which THIS jet and a flight-mate were both bound to a shot at once.
#                   For an AIM-120 flight the deferral rule keeps it near zero; the same file with
#                   the R-27R (pair-2v2-asym.fbm) is where the number becomes the finding
#   flt_defer_s     seconds this jet held its own trigger to keep the flight's cover
# and in events.log: `flight SORT_ASSIGN` (with src=cooperative|contract) and `flight COVER_DEFER`.
#
# MEASURED: the cooperative pair holds DIFFERENT targets in 1,036 of the 1,109 ticks in which both
# were assigned (93 %), and `dup && free` is 0 for all four units over the whole run. One AIM-120
# arrives 5.69 m from viper1 and fails six of its systems without taking engine, flight controls or
# structure — so all four are alive at t=600 and the verdict is TIMEOUT.
#
# THE CONTROL for all of it is the same file with the two `flight` lines deleted: the sort then has no
# flight to be a flight of, every flt_* column is inert, and both jets fly the single-ship intercept
# they flew before this round existed. [MESS] the control fires the same six rounds and lands NONE of
# them in 600 s.

unit viper1
  team friendly
  flight viper 1
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.40000 8000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 8.40000 8000 450
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

unit viper2
  team friendly
  flight viper 2
  module f16
  spawn 46.88334 6.40000 8150 90.0 450      # 1 nm right of lead's track, 150 m stacked = its station
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 8.40000 8000 450
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

unit bandit1
  team hostile
  flight bandit 1
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 7.85000 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 5.85000 8000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective survive

unit bandit2
  team hostile
  flight bandit 2
  module f16
  spawn 46.91666 7.85000 8150 270.0 450     # its own station: 1 nm right of ITS lead's track
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 5.85000 8000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective survive
